Description: boot setup of Legion: systemd-boot menu entries and a dracut initrd
 Every kernel installed by apt gets a classic systemd-boot menu entry from
 kernel-install, with an initrd built by dracut. The initrd runs systemd,
 so it finds an encrypted root partition without root= or crypttab, and it
 can unlock it with a FIDO2 security key.
 .
 When another package asks for a new initrd (the update-initramfs trigger,
 for example after a microcode update), the newest kernel gets a new initrd
 and menu entry. Older kernels stay untouched as a fallback. Boot counting
 is on: after three failed starts of a new entry, systemd-boot goes back to
 the previous kernel.

